msgid ""
"The Quarkus documentation has had a search feature for a long time,\n"
"but until now it was a simple substring search on the title and summary of "
"each guide.\n"
"It was better than nothing, but admittedly quite limited."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We've recently improved on that.\n"
"The https://quarkus.io/guides/[guides page] now provides actual full-text "
"search:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Among the (many!) improvements:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This is no longer a simple substring search, but state-of-the-art full-text "
"search,\n"
"with tokenization and text analysis (see how `vertx` matched `Vert.x` "
"above?)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Results are sorted by relevance,\n"
"thanks to the ability of full-text to assign a score to each hit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Search takes into account the title and summary of each guide,\n"
"but also the _full content of the guide's HTML page_."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Matching terms get highlighted in the list of results,\n"
"giving a glimpse of relevant content from each guide."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"And the best part? This new search is backed by a https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/search.quarkus.io[Quarkus app]!\n"
"It uses in particular the https://quarkus.io/guides/hibernate-search-orm-"
"elasticsearch[Hibernate Search extension],\n"
"which provides https://docs.jboss.org/hibernate/stable/search/reference/en-"
"US/html_single/#elasticsearch-integration[integration with OpenSearch/"
"Elasticsearch]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Stay tuned for more details in the coming weeks as we publish more blog "
"posts to dive into the implementation details.\n"
"In the meantime, happy searching!\n"
"And feel free to drop by in the comments below if you notice weird behavior "
"that you'd like to see fixed."
msgstr ""
